Lane served as a guardian of the Casterwill library in [[Paris, France]], alongside [[Dellix]]. The two of them permitted [[Sophie Casterwill]] to enter, without their intervention, upon seeing her enter the enchanted doorway which would only permit a member of the [[Casterwill family]] to pass. {{source|Memory Lane}}

Along with Lucas and Dellix, Lane later attacked the Huntik team when they returned to the library looking for information on the [[Willblade]]. Summoning her [[Wildwood Druid]] Titan, Lane and her team appeared to have the upper hand but this changed when Zhalia revealed her Titans hidden by her [[Thoughtspecter]] power. Lane revealed that they were searching for the location of an evil Amulet, [[Void]]. Lane later helped to rescue Lok and Sophie, and fought  off [[the Organization]] [[Suits]]. {{source|Chasing Void}}

Lane was present at the meeting of the [[Casterwill family]] at the [[Fortress of Iron Will]]. {{source|Sophie on Trial}} When a huge [[Blood Spiral]] army attacked, Lane and Dellix joined the Foundation and the Casterwills in their fight. They clashed with Lucas who wanted to figure out a way to escape, but Lane ultimately convinced Lucas to join them and help Dante's team. {{source|The Spiral War}}

Lane travelled with Lucas and Dellix to the [[Spiral Mark]] on a [[Scramjet]] driven by [[Scarlet Byrne]]. {{source|The Spiral Mark}} During the final battle against the [[Blood Spiral]], Lane was injured and rendered unconscious by a [[Psikofen]] Titan. {{source|Lok and the Betrayer}} She regained consciousness however and was seen celebrating with the rest of the Foundation and Casterwills following the defeat of [[the Betrayer]]. {{source|Dante's Return}}

